{
  "name": "batching",
  "integration": "audit-events-to-webhook",
  "script": "audit-events-to-webhook/audit-events-to-webhook.star",
  "description": "501 events, one past the 500-event batch boundary, so the delivery loop must issue TWO posts rather than one. This pins behaviour the README makes an explicit promise about -- 'events are sent 500 at a time, as several independent POSTs' -- which is the contract a receiver is written against. request_count==3 (one source read plus two deliveries) is the boundary assertion; a loop that sized its batch count with integer division would send one POST and silently drop 501 events, and one that sliced past the end would drop the tail. The three body_contains entries pin both ends of the walk: e001 opens the first batch, e500 closes it, and e501 exists only in the second. Rows are deliberately minimal -- the real models.Event shape is asserted in `happy`, and 501 full events would make this file unreadable for no extra coverage.",
